<title>NETHERLANDS: Hagemeyer 1996 net up 47.5 percent.</title>
<headline>Hagemeyer 1996 net up 47.5 percent.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yr to Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of guilders unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Net per shr (guilders)	     6.72 vs   5.90</p>
<p>    Net profit			   285.2  vs 193.3</p>
<p>    Dividend (guilders)		  2.28 vs   2.00</p>
<p>    Turnover (billions)		  8.22 vs   5.72</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts had expected Hagemeyer to post a net profit of between 262 million and 286 million guilders.  </p>
<p>    Operating profit		   447.6  vs 317.2</p>
<p>    Cash flow			    410.6  vs 278.8</p>
<p>NOTE - Hagemeyer said its 1996 dividend could be taken up either fully in cash or in the form of a stock dividend. Details on the stock dividend will be announced in the second week of April, 1997, it said.</p>
<p>Hong Kong's First Pacific Co has a controlling stake in Hagemeyer.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
